A 13-year-old teenager was injured in an attack by a shark while diving to catch the crab
Officials said the 13-year-old teenager was attacked and wounded by a shark on Saturday when he was catching crab while diving into California on the opening day of the lobster season.
The attack took place near Beacon Beach in Ansinitas before 7 a.m.
Chad Hummel from KSWB-TV, San Diego, said that on Saturday morning he had been diving with friends for about half an hour, at the same time he heard the sound of a boy screaming for help and after that he along with a group arrived to take him out of the water.
Hammell told that at first he felt that the boy had sounded in the excitement of catching the crab, but then he realized that he was screaming, 'Cutting me something!
I'm biting something!'
Hammel told that when he saw the boy, he found that the entire throat of the boy was torn.
"I made everyone's voice to get out of the water: there's a shark in the water!"
He was rushed to Ready Children's Hospital, San Diego, where his condition is stated to be critical.
Species of attacking sharks have not been traced.
Lifeguard Captain Larry Gilles said in a conversation with the media that a shark was detected in the area a few weeks ago, but it was found that it is not a dangerous species of shark.
Gills further deposed that that the upper spot of the torso of the victim is seriously injured.
