HIV/AIDS: According to the report, there has been a 14% increase in new cases in China
China has announced that there has been an increase of 14 per cent in people suffering from HIV and AIDS in the country.
Health officials have said that more than 820,000 people across the country are suffering from this disease.
Only in the second quarter of 2018, about 40,000 new cases were reported.
In view of the changes in the recent past, the reason for most of the new cases is said to be sex.
Traditionally, HIV is spreading rapidly in some parts of China due to infected blood infection.
At a conference in Yunnan province, Chinese health officials said that the number of people who suffered through HIV had become almost zero.
However, the number of people suffering from HIV and AIDS in China has increased by 100,000 every year.
HIV infection is a serious problem due to sex performed by China's LGBT community.
In 1997, homosexuality was promoted in China, but it is reported that there is considerable discrimination against the LGBT community.
Due to the country's orthodox importance by studies, it is estimated that 70-90% of men who have sex with men will finally marry women.
Due to many infections of the disease, there is an insufficient protection about sex in these relationships.
Since 2003, the Chinese government has tried to solve this problem, for which every person has been promised that they will be given access to HIV medicine.
